---
# Renders infra/gcp/packer/setup.sh: the generic Debian/apt base-package
# bootstrap (Docker + prerequisites) for the beam4pm_pro Packer image build,
# extracted from the single /tmp/beam4pm-provision.sh heredoc in
# packer-beam4pm-image.pkr.hcl.tmpl into a real sibling file uploaded via a
# "file" provisioner and executed by a sibling "shell" provisioner -- the
# BEAMOps/PragProg script-separation pattern.
#
# Fully static: zero b4pi:PackerImage facts are needed (the Debian package
# names and the systemd bootstrap step are the same regardless of which
# image/container this build is for), so this template carries no sparql:
# block. Body is wrapped in {% raw %} as defensive/documentary practice for
# a zero-Tera-variable shell script, matching mermaid-pack/templates/
# render_mermaid.sh.tmpl's convention for the same case.
#
# The remaining, genuinely fact-driven provisioning (docker pull of
# ${var.container_image}, the systemd unit install/enable, the provenance
# facts write) stays inline in packer-beam4pm-image.pkr.hcl.tmpl as a
# content=<<-EOT heredoc -- Packer's "file" provisioner does not run HCL
# interpolation over an externally-sourced file's bytes, only over strings
# literally inside the .pkr.hcl config, so ${var.container_image} cannot
# move here without breaking the build-time image-override capability
# documented on b4pi:packerContainerImage / the container_image variable.
to: infra/gcp/packer/setup.sh
force: true
---
{% raw %}#!/usr/bin/env bash
# GENERATED by ggen (beam4pm-pro-infra-pack/templates/packer-setup.sh.tmpl). Do not edit.
set -euo pipefail

echo "=== beam4pm_pro setup: base OS packages ==="

export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
apt-get update
apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends docker.io ca-certificates curl
systemctl enable --now docker

echo "=== beam4pm_pro setup: base OS packages complete ==="
{% endraw %}
